{"type": "message", "id": "89b7452c", "parentId": "04bda551", "timestamp": "2026-04-06T20:11:19.387Z", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_4a53d614e263432ea157ca0a", "toolName": "web_search", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\n  \"query\": \"\\\"Goldsmiths\\\" \\\"MA\\\" \\\"international tuition\\\" \\\"2025\\\"\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 2,\n  \"tookMs\": 855,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f5ac5bddc8db1dea\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nGoldsmiths, University of London - The UK Study Expert\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f5ac5bddc8db1dea\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://theukstudyexpert.com/universities/goldsmithslondon/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d39e768801ce72b9\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nGoldsmiths utilizes AP, IB, and SAT/ACT test results for admissions purposes only. No advanced entry or course credit will be awarded. We will superscore both the ACT and the SAT. ... International Foundation Certificate (Arts and Humanities, Computing, Media, Culture and Society, Music Computing, Social Sciences) International Foundation Certificate (Design, Management and Psychology, Music)\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d39e768801ce72b9\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"December 8, 2025\",\n      \"siteName\": \"theukstudyexpert.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"8849cad62bbe76a0\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nr/UniUK on Reddit: Goldsmiths 2025??\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"8849cad62bbe76a0\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.reddit.com/r/UniUK/comments/1n7prng/goldsmiths_2025/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c10c0f253c533423\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nI am shocked (and pleased!) that they would give you some credit for your previous schooling. Honestly, I’ve never heard of that happening. I know Goldsmiths is in tough fiscal straights (like many many UK unis), so perhaps they figure two years of international tuition is better than none.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c10c0f253c533423\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"September 3, 2025\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.reddit.com\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}], "details": {"query": "\"Goldsmiths\" \"MA\" \"international tuition\" \"2025\"", "provider": "brave", "count": 2, "tookMs": 855, "externalContent": {"untrusted": true, "source": "web_search", "provider": "brave", "wrapped": true}, "results": [{"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"f5ac5bddc8db1dea\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nGoldsmiths, University of London - The UK Study Expert\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"f5ac5bddc8db1dea\">>>", "url": "https://theukstudyexpert.com/universities/goldsmithslondon/", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"d39e768801ce72b9\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nGoldsmiths utilizes AP, IB, and SAT/ACT test results for admissions purposes only. No advanced entry or course credit will be awarded. We will superscore both the ACT and the SAT. ... International Foundation Certificate (Arts and Humanities, Computing, Media, Culture and Society, Music Computing, Social Sciences) International Foundation Certificate (Design, Management and Psychology, Music)\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"d39e768801ce72b9\">>>", "published": "December 8, 2025", "siteName": "theukstudyexpert.com"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"8849cad62bbe76a0\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nr/UniUK on Reddit: Goldsmiths 2025??\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"8849cad62bbe76a0\">>>", "url": "https://www.reddit.com/r/UniUK/comments/1n7prng/goldsmiths_2025/", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"c10c0f253c533423\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nI am shocked (and pleased!) that they would give you some credit for your previous schooling. Honestly, I’ve never heard of that happening. I know Goldsmiths is in tough fiscal straights (like many many UK unis), so perhaps they figure two years of international tuition is better than none.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"c10c0f253c533423\">>>", "published": "September 3, 2025", "siteName": "www.reddit.com"}]}, "isError": false, "timestamp": 1775506279385}}
